From: JeongBong Seo <lifeofthanks@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bound per-path Mamba checkpoints by minimax replay coverage

Apply after 0011 on SGLang v0.5.18. Keep the newest frontier and minimize
the resulting whole-path maximum replay gap when selecting an old victim.
Break ties by integer uniform-quantile deviation, then prefer older history.
Protect forks, locks, session references, reused states, load-back pins and
device leaves. Keep the existing post-BackupKV action ordering and soft cap.

Global pressure eviction, inter-path fairness, exact-demand allocation and
Full KV eviction are unchanged. This release has no Rust radix-tree backend.
Includes focused tests and a synthetic CPU policy A/B, not GPU serving claims.

